# Pith — environment example
#
# Pith ships with NO required environment variables. createEngine() works
# key-free with in-memory defaults. Everything below is opt-in for the features
# that need an external provider. Copy to `.env` and fill in only what you use.
#
# Pith NEVER assumes a billable provider by default — extract/search throw
# NotConfiguredError until you pass a backend explicitly.

# --- Structured extraction (enables engine.extract) -----------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions endpoint (OpenAI, Groq, Together,
# OpenRouter, vLLM/Ollama, Anthropic's OpenAI-compat layer, …).
# EXTRACTION_API_KEY=
# EXTRACTION_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# EXTRACTION_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# --- Web search (enables engine.search via the Brave backend) -------------
# BRAVE_API_KEY=

# --- HTTP face auth (optional) -------------------------------------------
# The @use-pith/core/http face has NO auth by default. If you gate it behind an
# api-key header, consumers send it as `x-api-key`. No value is seeded.
# PITH_API_KEY=

# --- Freshness tiers (opt-in, per-request via freshnessTier) --------------
# Override the default catalog (news=3600s, standard=86400s) by passing
# createEngine({ freshnessTierCatalog: {...} }). No env var required.
